        "subheadline_text_strong_accented": false,
        "text": "<p>Unlock your potential in the fitness industry with Study Active's accredited Pilates Instructor course. Start your journey today! </p><p>If you’re wondering how to become a Pilates instructor, the good news is that there is a clear path into this growing area of the fitness industry. With the right Pilates instructor course, you can gain the knowledge, practical skills, and recognised qualification needed to teach safe and effective mat-based Pilates sessions. </p><p>Pilates instructors help clients improve posture, core strength, flexibility, balance, and overall movement control. They work in gyms, health clubs, boutique studios, community settings, and online, making this a flexible and rewarding career choice for people who are passionate about fitness and wellbeing. </p><p>To become a Pilates instructor in the UK, you will typically need a recognised <a href=\"https://studyactive.co.uk/products/active-iq-level-3-diploma-in-instructing-pilates-matwork\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Level 3 Pilates qualification</span></a> that gives you the skills to plan, deliver, and adapt classes for a range of clients. In this guide, we’ll explain the qualifications you need, the skills that matter most, expected salaries, and the steps to start your career. </p>",
