    "v2_text_plus_image_Q3MpEb": {
      "type": "v2_text-plus-image",
      "name": "t:lesections.textplusimage.presets.name",
      "settings": {
        "image": "shopify://shop_images/Blog_Post_-_Pilates_3.png",
        "heading_text": "<p>What is a Pilates Instructor?</p>",
        "heading_type": "h3",
        "heading_size": "h3",
        "heading_no_decal": false,
        "heading_decal_left": false,
        "heading_strong_accented": true,
        "subheadline_text": "",
        "subheadline_text_size": "copy-l",
        "subheadline_text_no_decal": false,
        "subheadline_text_strong_accented": false,
        "text": "<p>A <strong>Pilates instructor</strong> teaches structured exercise sessions designed to improve core strength, flexibility, posture, and overall movement control. </p><p>Using a combination of controlled movements and breathing techniques, Pilates instructors help clients develop better body awareness and reduce the risk of injury. Sessions can be delivered in group classes or on a one-to-one basis, depending on the client’s goals and experience level. </p><p>Pilates instructors are responsible for planning safe and effective sessions, demonstrating exercises with correct technique, and adapting movements to suit different abilities. This includes supporting beginners, working with clients returning from injury, and helping more advanced participants progress their training. </p><p>As a qualified instructor, you can work in a variety of environments, including gyms, health clubs, boutique studios, and online platforms - giving you flexibility in how and where you build your career. </p>",
        "text_size": "copy-l",
        "text_no_decal": false,
        "text_strong_accented": false,
        "claim_text": "",
        "claim_text_size": "copy-l",
